meta { title = "Project manifests", description = "Configure an application entry point and local source libraries.", order = 2, group = "Using Kalandra" }

Use kalandra new for a starter, or create the files shown here. The manifest selects the source entry and any local package mappings. It is compiler input, not a file loaded by the generated application.

h2 { "A minimal application" }

Use a new working directory. Create my-app/src and save this as my-app/src/main.k:

codeblock { language = kalandra, """from "std/io" import println, IoError
from "std/fmt" import format

fn main() -> unit ! IoError:
  output: i64 = 6 * 7

  try println(format("{}", output))
  return ()
""" }

Save this manifest as my-app/kalandra.toml:

codeblock { language = toml, """format = 1

[project]
entry = "src/main.k"
""" }

codeblock { language = bash, """kalandra-check --project my-app/kalandra.toml
kalandra --project my-app/kalandra.toml -o my-app/program
./my-app/program
""" }

Select either a source path or --project, not both. There is no implicit ancestor search for a project manifest. Relative entry/package paths resolve from the canonical manifest directory; -o still resolves from the current working directory.

The program returns 42.

h2 { "Map a local source library" }

Create my-app/lib, save this library as my-app/lib/geometry.k, and replace the application entry with the second example:

codeblock { language = kalandra, """export fn area(width: i64, height: i64) -> i64:
  return width * height
""" }

codeblock { language = kalandra, """from "std/io" import println, IoError
from "std/fmt" import format

from "geometry" import area

fn main() -> unit ! IoError:
  output: i64 = area(6, 7)

  try println(format("{}", output))
  return ()
""" }

Replace my-app/kalandra.toml with:

codeblock { language = toml, """format = 1

[project]
entry = "src/main.k"

[packages]
geometry = "lib/geometry.k"
""" }

Check and build again using the commands above; the result remains 42. Code in the application may then import exported declarations from "geometry". Mapping a name does not make private declarations public. Explicit mappings are offline source locations, separate from managed Git dependencies.

h2 { "A source library manifest" }

codeblock { language = toml, """format = 1

[package]
name = "geometry"
version = "0.2.0"
entry = "src/public.k"
""" }

Save that library manifest in a separate library root, with the exported area function above in src/public.k. A source library declares the module callers import and resolves its own dependencies. Its entry and local mappings must stay within its canonical root. Version metadata does not introduce version-range solving.

h2 { "Import a system library" }

In an application manifest, add a system library to the existing dependencies table.

code { """sqlite = { system = "sqlite3" }""" }

Use the name on the left in an import. For example, import sqlite3_libversion_number from "sqlite" and call sqlite3_libversion_number() to get SQLite's version as an integer. The host compiler locates the installed public header and links the library. For a library you build with your project, give its header and object or library paths relative to the manifest.

code { """bytes = { header = "bytes.h", library = "bytes.o" }""" }

A C binding can expose 32-bit and 64-bit scalar numbers and functions returning void. On Linux, Windows and macOS, a C function can borrow ByteBuffer contents for the duration of a call. The following header uses a Clang diagnostic to bind both pointers to the byte count n. Clang can diagnose undersized objects in C calls when their size is known. Kalandra also checks dynamically sized buffers at runtime.

codeblock { language = c, """#include <stddef.h>
#include <stdint.h>

#define BYTE_EXTENT(p, n) __attribute__((diagnose_if((n) > __builtin_object_size((p), 0), "byte count exceeds buffer", "error")))

void copyPrefix(size_t n,
                uint8_t * _Nonnull dst __attribute__((noescape)),
                const uint8_t * _Nonnull src __attribute__((noescape)))
    BYTE_EXTENT(dst, n) BYTE_EXTENT(src, n);
""" }

Apple SDK bindings may also use counted_by on pointer parameters with a bounds-safety-capable Xcode.

In Kalandra, import copyPrefix from "bytes" and call it with two initialized buffers.

code { """try copyPrefix(2, dst, src)""" }

If either buffer contains fewer than two bytes, the call returns BufferError.OutOfRange before entering C. Reserving capacity does not initialize bytes. The destination requires an exclusive borrow. The source is passed as a read-only snapshot. A zero-length borrow supplies a non-null address for the duration of the call.

The binding author is responsible for matching the linked implementation to the header. The C function must stay within the declared bounds. It may neither free the borrowed storage nor retain its address after returning. Pointer returns, ownership transfer, callbacks and Objective-C object receivers require additional lifetime rules and cannot be imported. Native imports target host CPU executables.

h2 { "Build modes" }

codeblock { language = bash, """kalandra --project my-app/kalandra.toml -O2 -o program
./program
""" }

The optimized CPU program also displays 42. CPU builds produce an executable. GPU builds produce an application directory containing the executable and its backend resources; keep those files together. Shape, numeric and error checks remain part of the native semantics in optimized builds.

